\input{abstract}
\end{abstract}
\section{Introduction}
Rice production in the Mekong Delta faces tightening dry-season water allocations and rising scrutiny of methane emissions.
Alternate wetting and drying has been promoted as a water-saving practice, but adoption lags behind the evidence.
\section{Methods}
We coordinated a three-season trial across six sites spanning the upper and lower delta.
Extension staff coached participating farmers on safe water-level thresholds.
